    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418-a1">

                <pb facs="0783" n="673" xml:id="pg673"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 469.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Colonel Stewart to Mr. Pratt.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tabreez</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 21,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    this day of Your Excellency’s dispatch No. 2, dated 14th June, 1890.</p>
                <p>I have already summoned the woman Asli to appear as a witness, but I fear she
                    will, at the trial, deny her previous statement, as I hear she has told Dr.
                    Cochran she will give no evidence in the matter.</p>
                <p>Mr. Mechlin has just arrived, also Theodore, the late Mrs. Wright’s brother, and
                    a man who saw Minas running away from Mr. Wright’s house on the afternoon of the
                    14th May, just after the murder, with a dagger in his hand. The other witnesses
                    are en route.</p>
                <p>I have summoned Dr. Shedd, to whom Minas confessed the murder of Mrs. Wright and
                    asked him to pray for his soul, so I shall have ample evidence.</p>
                <p>With reference, to the last part of your letter under reply, I am aware that,
                    according to Mohammedan law, the causing the death of a child of a pregnant
                    woman is murder, and this child, having been a son in a well-formed state, I
                    shall, as directed in your letter, press home this charge, and have full
                    evidence to prove it. I had, however, intended to do this previous to the
                    receipt of your letter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. E. Stewart</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Colonel, Her Majesty’s Consul-General,
                        Tabreez</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
